      <slug></slug>
      <title>A rubyist&#39;s naive comparison of some database systems and toolkits</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Ruby + Rails</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will be a quick comparison of some of the many relational and non relational database systems that can be used with ruby.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I will focus on features, syntax and performance. This is not a talk by a database expert but simply a modest attempt to show the differences between some of the possibilities offered and clear things up a bit.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2681">Marc Lainez</person>
      </persons>
